{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 33, :comments ["Mount of YHWH — for they had not yet moved from opposite Mount Horev, which is in the wilderness of Sinai, and this was after the Tabernacle was set up, as I explained above. And in any case, they had been at Mount Sinai until now." "A journey of three days — they traveled for three full days, for they did not camp until the end of the three, and because of the exertion of the journey, the people were as murmurers, as we find in the section of the red heifer: ״ותקצר נפש העם בדרך וידבר העם באלהים ובמשה״." "And the ark of the covenant of YHWH traveled before them — all those three days, to seek out for them a resting place, for the cloud traveled above the ark."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {1 "Rashbam cites Numbers 21:5 but writes וידבר העם באלהים ובמשה; the received text of that verse reads וידבר העם באלהים ובמשה, though some witnesses there have the singular וידבר."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:49:58.687705979Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}